  📗
    The file at *path* as the answer to *r*. The path is the handler's own
    and nothing about it is checked: for a name that a client supplied, use
    the form that takes a directory and a name.

    A 404 when there is no file there. Otherwise a 200 with the file as its
    body, sent in pieces so that a large file is never held in memory, with
    the media type of its name, Last-Modified, an ETag made of its size and
    the time it was changed, and Accept-Ranges. A 304 when *r* shows that the
    client has it. For a GET with one Range of bytes, a 206 with that part,
    or a 416 when the file has no such bytes. A Range that asks for several
    parts, or cannot be read, is ignored.
